course: dictionary
lesson: 257
title: Alter means change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To alter something is to change it, usually a little. A tailor can alter trousers so they fit better, and a plan can be altered when it rains. Alter is a verb, so it has forms like alters, altered and altering.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «He was indeed an altered Toad!» Toad is still Toad, but something about him has changed. Altered means changed.
explain: Test your meaning. Swap in «changed» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: To alter something means to change it, usually a little.
fact: If something alters, it becomes different.
fact: To alter clothes means to make them fit better, for example by shortening them.
fact: In maths, «if you alter one number» the answer may change.
fact: In 1299 the money-changers' guild of Florence banned the new digits in account books, fearing they were easy to alter.
exercise: «The tailor will alter the trousers so they fit.» What does alter mean here? | To throw them away | To wash them in hot water | *To change them so they fit better | To put them in a box
exercise: «He was indeed an altered Toad!» What does altered mean? | Hidden | *Changed | Asleep | Lost
exercise: Dad says, «We must alter our plan because of the rain.» Which word means the same as alter? | Stop | Repeat | Forget | *Change
test: «If you alter one number, the answer may change.» What may happen to the answer? | It will always stay the same | It turns into a word | *It may change | It disappears
test: What is the best way to check that you have the right meaning of a new word? | Look only at the title | Pick the longest answer | Ignore the sentence and guess | *Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense
exam: Which sentence uses alter to mean make something different? | *Rain may alter our walk to school | I like the colour blue | The ball is round | She ran to the shop
